<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 15:25:38 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>考古学家发现了一个新石器时代的人类骑着豹子的雕塑，这“与我们以前遇到过的任何东西都不一样”</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-uncover-a-neolithic-sculpture-of-a-human-riding-a-leopard-thats-unlike-anything-we-have-encountered-before-180989477/</link><description>这件文物是在土耳其东南部一处拥有 11,000 年历史的卡拉汉泰佩 (Karahan Tepe) 遗址的挖掘过程中发现的。这座 2.3 英尺高的雕塑早在文字发明之前就已创作，其用途仍是一个谜</description><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 14:09:55 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-uncover-a-neolithic-sculpture-of-a-human-riding-a-leopard-thats-unlike-anything-we-have-encountered-before-180989477/</guid></item><item><title>考古学家在波兰挖掘罗马时代墓地时惊讶地发现了一条由 42 颗牙齿制成的 5000 年前项链</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-excavating-a-roman-era-cemetery-in-poland-were-surprised-to-stumble-upon-a-5000-year-old-necklace-made-of-42-teeth-180989471/</link><description>这些珠宝由狼、鹿、熊甚至人类等大型哺乳动物的牙齿制成，是在波兰南部的一座坟墓中发现的，该坟墓可能属于绳纹器文化的一位重要族长</description><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 21:05:23 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-excavating-a-roman-era-cemetery-in-poland-were-surprised-to-stumble-upon-a-5000-year-old-necklace-made-of-42-teeth-180989471/</guid></item><item><title>令研究人员惊讶的是，这种巨型恐龙在寒冷的气候下产卵</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/to-researchers-surprise-this-giant-dinosaur-laid-eggs-in-a-cold-climate-180989474/</link><description>一项新的研究表明，泰坦巨龙利用腐烂的植被来为它们的蛋保暖，就像今天的鳄鱼一样</description><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 20:29:56 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/to-researchers-surprise-this-giant-dinosaur-laid-eggs-in-a-cold-climate-180989474/</guid></item><item><title>这艘医院船在第二次世界大战期间在阿尔巴尼亚海岸沉没。现在，这里充满了海洋生物</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-hospital-ship-sank-off-albania-coast-during-world-war-ii-now-its-teeming-with-marine-life-180989468/</link><description>对“波”号的一项新调查揭示了欣欣向荣的水下生态系统，其中包括稀有的地中海僧海豹</description><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 17:57:33 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-hospital-ship-sank-off-albania-coast-during-world-war-ii-now-its-teeming-with-marine-life-180989468/</guid></item><item><title>世界上最大的连环杀手“杀人狂”收藏（从约翰·韦恩·盖西到 HH·福尔摩斯）在芝加哥开幕</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/worlds-largest-collection-of-serial-killer-murderabilia-from-john-wayne-gacy-to-hh-holmes-opens-in-chicago-180989461/</link><description>令人毛骨悚然的新展览将展出 2,000 多件属于或与来自世界各地约 150 名连环杀手有关的物品</description><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 14:24:18 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/worlds-largest-collection-of-serial-killer-murderabilia-from-john-wayne-gacy-to-hh-holmes-opens-in-chicago-180989461/</guid></item><item><title>偷孩子们的糖果、防溅小便池和埋内裤，天哪！这是 2026 年搞笑诺贝尔奖的获得者</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/stealing-candy-from-children-splash-proof-urinals-and-buried-panties-oh-my-here-are-the-winners-of-the-2026-ig-nobel-prizes-180989463/</link><description>这些奖项是对诺贝尔奖的无关联的恶搞。它们强调了令人惊讶且听起来很愚蠢的研究成果，但也让人们思考</description><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 20:50:44 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/stealing-candy-from-children-splash-proof-urinals-and-buried-panties-oh-my-here-are-the-winners-of-the-2026-ig-nobel-prizes-180989463/</guid></item><item><title>窃贼闯入法国博物馆并盗走价值超过 250 万美元的雷诺阿画作</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/thieves-broke-into-a-french-museum-and-made-off-with-renoir-paintings-worth-more-than-25-million-180989462/</link><description>今天早些时候，窃贼从法国里维埃拉的雷诺阿博物馆偷走了四